There were 180 10% configs.

From "shell", we can see that from at least config 156
onwards the random cell seed was 370+#Config.

This is not too important for reproducing the results however,
given that we are interested in robust statistical averages,
resampling with different random seeds will not change the results anyway

In config1 we have an example output of the eigen values from our Hamiltonian
diagonalisation code jdqr.m, eigenwerte2_electrons.m, eigenwerte2_holes.m
